+}
+
+SHIPPING_DIFFICULTY = "hard"
+
+CERTIFICATE_LANGUAGE = {
+    "description": (
+        "A list of exactly n integer user identifiers in 0..q-1, in step order; "
+        "the explicitly singleton-authorized anchor step must use its one "
+        "authorized user, while every other step may use any of the q users."
+    ),
+    "bounds": {
+        "entries": "n",
+        "entry_min": 0,
+        "entry_max": "q-1",
+        "anchor_authorizations": 1,
+        "shipping_n": 120,
+        "shipping_q": 1000003,
+    },
+}
+
+STRUCTURAL_HINT = (
+    "The user assignment is affine over Z_q in the displayed scalar step labels."
+)
+PLACEBO_HINT = (
+    "The user assignment rewards careful tracking of the displayed modular workflow constraints."
+)
+
+NOTES = """\
+Section 2, especially Definitions 2.1 and 2.2 and Sections 2.2--2.3, fixes the
+native object: a plan is a function from workflow steps to users, authorization
+is a step-user relation, and a Type-1 entailment constraint (rho,s,t) is checked
+by membership of (plan(s),plan(t)) in the displayed binary user relation. Here
+rho_d is the finite relation {(u,v): v-u = d mod q}; no SAT, graph, or finite-field
+surrogate replaces the workflow presented to the solver.
+
+The easy-method audit is decisive. Section 3 gives FPT algorithms for regular
+constraints, Section 4 contrasts these with W[1]-hard arbitrary relations, and
+Theorem 4.2 gives only an ETH worst-case lower bound for a different two-user
+subcase. None proves this planted distribution hard. Moreover, this module's
+special rho_d constraints are solved directly by linear-time propagation on a
+connected constraint system. It is therefore Track B, never Track A. The
+reference algorithm is implemented, timed, and reported as succeeding 8/8.
+
+Generation is inverse: sample a non-small affine slope and distinct scalar labels,
+compute the plan, then add only difference relations induced by that plan. A
+random spanning tree makes propagation complete; extra constraints are sampled
+from the same pair distribution and shuffled, so tree relations have no marker.
+The attacks try per-step label identity, lowest-authorized greedy assignment,
+small affine slopes, randomized one-pass propagation, and 256 random affine
+restarts. Canonicalization uses intrinsic labels, reverses relation orientation
+canonically, normalizes every offset by one canonical nonzero offset, and is
+invariant under step renumbering, constraint order/reversal, and every affine
+relabeling u -> r*u+t of the modular user set.
+"""
+
+
+# Filled after the script-owned oracle runs. selftest reads no transcript files.
+_G9_ARMS = {
+    "bare": {"solved": 0, "attempts": 0},
+    "hinted": {"solved": 0, "attempts": 0},
+    "placebo": {"solved": 0, "attempts": 0},
+}
+_G9_HINTED_VERDICT = "pending"
